{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block title %}Deep dives: every question and the scoreboard · The Referee{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The question-by-question rulings behind the evidence, with the scoreboard of the main arguments as posted and in their best version.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<p class="crumb"><a href="{{ base }}">Home</a> › Deep dives</p>
<h1>Deep dives</h1>
<p class="lede">{{ n_questions }} debate questions and {{ n_claims }} rated claims from r/DebateAChristian, each graded with the public rubric. These are the working notes behind the evidence lists on the home page.</p>

<section aria-labelledby="scoreboard-h">
  <h2 id="scoreboard-h">Scoreboard: the main arguments as posted</h2>
  <table class="scoreboard">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Argument</th><th scope="col">As usually stated</th><th scope="col">Best version</th><th scope="col">Weakest point</th><th scope="col">In short</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for row in site.scoreboard %}
    <tr>
      <td class="arg">{{ row.argument }}</td>
      <td data-label="As usually stated">{{ m.meter(row.as_posted) }}</td>
      <td data-label="Best version">{{ m.meter(row.best_version) }}</td>
      <td class="weak" data-label="Weakest point">{{ row.weakest_point }}</td>
      <td class="sum" data-label="In short">{{ row.summary }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="small">Both columns move only when a ruling changes, and every change is in the file history on GitHub.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="questions-h" id="questions">
  <h2 id="questions-h">Every question</h2>
  <ul class="qlist">
  {% for q in questions %}
    <li><a href="{{ base }}q/{{ q.id }}/"><span class="qn">Q{{ q.n }}</span> <span class="qt">{{ q.title }}</span></a> <span class="pct">{{ q.confidence }}%</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="small">% = how confident the referee is that the ruling is right, not that the claim is true.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="big-h" class="box">
  <h2 id="big-h">The big question</h2>
  <p><b>Was Jesus the Son of God?</b> No single number. It depends on three inputs you choose: how likely God is at all, how likely a resurrection is if God exists, and how likely divinity is if he rose. The historical facts most scholars grant are on the <a href="{{ base }}about/#history">About page</a>.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
